Package: video-hevc-converter
Version: @VERSION@
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10),
 python3-venv,
 python3-pip,
 ffmpeg,
 adduser,
 systemd
Recommends: intel-media-va-driver-non-free,
 intel-gpu-tools,
 vainfo
Maintainer: buianhhuy96 <buianhhuy96@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/buianhhuy96/Video_HEVC_Converter
Description: Video HEVC Converter background service
 Native systemd service that scans configured folders, transcodes non-HEVC
 videos to HEVC using Intel QSV (with libx265 fallback), validates the
 result, and atomically replaces the original. Includes a FastAPI web UI
 on port 8080 (open by default; set UI_PASSWORD to require HTTP Basic
 auth).
 .
 The service runs as the "video-converter" system user in the render and
 video groups (for /dev/dri access). Config lives in
 /var/lib/video-hevc-converter/config.yaml.
